  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Cgi Federal obligated $1.1B in FY2026 to date across 271 awards. Cgi Federal averaged $4.1M per award and obligations were down 7.8% year over year. Cgi Federal received the largest share of its FY2026 to date obligations from the Department of State at $235M, followed by the General Services Administration at $181M and the Department of Justice at $139M. Cgi Federal won the bulk of work in IT and services markets: Other Computer Related Services accounted for $462M, Computer Systems Design Services accounted for $212M, and Computer Facilities Management Services accounted for $202M. Historical obligations show Cgi Federal at $1B in FY21, $1.1B in FY22, $1.1B in FY23, $1.2B in FY24, $1.2B in FY25, and $1.1B in FY26. The FY2026 to date totals are partial, fiscal year to date, and the figures for largest awards and expiring contracts, where listed elsewhere, represent total contract values rather than yearly obligations.",
